.TH std::move_iterator::move_iterator 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::move_iterator::move_iterator \- std::move_iterator::move_iterator

.SH Synopsis
move_iterator();                                \fB(1)\fP (constexpr since C++17)
explicit move_iterator( iterator_type x );      \fB(2)\fP (constexpr since C++17)
template< class U >                             \fB(3)\fP (constexpr since C++17)
move_iterator( const move_iterator<U>& other );

Constructs a new move_iterator.

                         Overload            current
                         \fB(1)\fP      value-initialized
                                  initialized with
                                  x
                         \fB(2)\fP      \fI(until C++20)\fP
                                  std::move(x)
                                  \fI(since C++20)\fP
                         \fB(3)\fP      initialized with other.current

3) The converting constructor.

If U is not convertible to Iter, the program is ill-formed.                  \fI(until C++20)\fP
This overload participates in overload resolution only if std::is_same_v<U,  \fI(since C++20)\fP
Iter> is false and std::convertible_to<const U&, Iter> is modeled.

.SH Parameters

x     - iterator to adapt
other - iterator adaptor to copy

